## Filtering for Better Analysis

### Date Range Filtering

Select the right time period for your analysis goals:

<Tabs>
  <Tab title="Recent Activity">
    **Last 7-30 days**
    
    ✅ **Best for:**
    - Current performance monitoring
    - Recent changes evaluation
    - Short-term trend analysis
    - Quick health checks
  </Tab>
  
  <Tab title="Monthly Analysis">
    **Single month period**
    
    ✅ **Best for:**
    - Monthly performance reviews
    - Periodic reporting
    - Month-over-month comparisons
    - Seasonal patterns
  </Tab>
  
  <Tab title="Extended Period">
    **Multiple months**
    
    ✅ **Best for:**
    - Long-term trend analysis
    - Strategic planning
    - Comprehensive reviews
    - Historical comparisons
    
    <Warning>
    Remember the 250 conversation limit. Longer periods may hit this limit, analyzing only the most recent 250 conversations.
    </Warning>
  </Tab>
</Tabs>

---

### User Filtering

Focus your analysis on specific users:

| Filter Option | Use Case | Best For |
|--------------|----------|----------|
| **All Users** | Organization-wide analysis | General performance, broad trends |
| **Specific User** | Individual user tracking | Support cases, VIP customers, issue investigation |
| **User Cohorts** | Group behavior analysis | Beta testers, user segments, team tracking |

<Tip>
**Pro Tip:** Start with "All Users" to get the big picture, then create focused analyses for specific users or periods where you notice interesting patterns.
</Tip>

---

## Working with the 250 Conversation Limit

<Warning>
**Maximum: 250 Conversations per Analysis**

If your filters match more than 250 conversations, only the most recent 250 will be analyzed.
</Warning>

### Strategies for Large Datasets

<AccordionGroup>
  <Accordion title="Time-Based Segmentation" icon="calendar">
    **Break into smaller time periods**
    
    Instead of analyzing 3 months at once:
    - Week 1: Jan 1-7
    - Week 2: Jan 8-15
    - Week 3: Jan 16-23
    - Continue as needed
    
    Then compare insights across periods to identify trends.
  </Accordion>
  
  <Accordion title="User-Based Segmentation" icon="user">
    **Analyze users separately**
    
    - Run analysis for User Group A
    - Run analysis for User Group B  
    - Run analysis for User Group C
    
    Compare results to understand different user experiences.
  </Accordion>
  
  <Accordion title="Priority-Based Approach" icon="star">
    **Focus on what matters most**
    
    Filter for:
    - Failed conversations only
    - High-value users
    - Specific issues or topics
    - Recent critical period
    
    Let the system analyze the most important 250 conversations.
  </Accordion>
</AccordionGroup>

---

## Variability in AI Results

<Info>
**Understanding AI Estimation:**

The system warns that "analysis results are estimates generated by AI and may vary between different analysis runs."
</Info>

### Why Results Vary

AI analysis is not deterministic because:

1. **Interpretation**: AI models interpret language context differently each time
2. **Sampling**: With 250+ conversations, slight variations in which are prioritized
3. **Model Updates**: AI models improve over time, affecting analysis
4. **Pattern Detection**: AI may emphasize different patterns on different runs

### Best Practices

<Check>
**How to get consistent insights:**
- Run analyses at regular intervals (e.g., weekly)
- Track trends over time rather than single runs
- Focus on major patterns, not minor details
- Combine AI insights with manual review
- Use specific filters to reduce variability
</Check>

